# Pinned tool versions. Bump a version here and in one PR, never ad hoc.
#
# templ is pinned in go.mod via the `tool` directive (Go 1.24+) and is NOT
# listed here; `go tool templ` is the only supported way to run it. The version
# below is what CI asserts go.mod resolves to.
TEMPL_VERSION=v0.3.1020

# DataStar 1.0 stable syntax: data-on:click, not the beta data-on-click form.
DATASTAR_VERSION=1.0.4

# Tailwind v4 standalone CLI. No Node anywhere in the toolchain: the generated
# CSS is committed, so `go build` never needs this binary.
# https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/releases
TAILWIND_VERSION=4.1.16

# golangci-lint, used by `make lint`. The version is not "whatever is current"
# — it has to be able to read this module. golangci-lint refuses to load a
# config for a module whose `go` directive names a newer Go language version
# than the one it was built with, and it exits 3 with a message that reads like
# a misconfiguration rather than a version mismatch. The pin is 2.14.0 because
# that is what reports itself as built with go1.27.0, which is above go.mod's
# `go 1.26.0`. 2.5.0 was built with go1.25 and could not read this module at
# all, so `make lint` never analysed a single file.
#
# When the `go` directive in go.mod moves up a minor version, this pin has to
# move with it, and the check is the first line of `golangci-lint version`: if
# it is lower than the module's Go version, the lint job is not linting.
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=2.14.0

# Trivy, installed by aquasecurity/trivy-action in the `trivy-fs` job. The
# action has a `version` input defaulting to a value frozen when the action was
# released, and that release's assets no longer exist upstream, so the scanner
# died at install with an exit 1 and no scan. A default that is a version
# string in someone else's release is the same unpinned download as `uses: @…`
# without a SHA: it rots silently and the job reports a scanner failure rather
# than a version that has gone. Stated here so the pin is reviewable in one
# place. A working asset was verified for this version:
# https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/download/v0.74.0/trivy_0.74.0_Linux-64bit.tar.gz
TRIVY_VERSION=0.74.0

# Pa11y CI, for the accessibility gate. Runs against a booted server.
# Consumed by scripts/pa11y.sh and .github/workflows/quality.yml; pa11y-ci 4.x
# needs an even-numbered Node of 20 or above, which is what NODE_VERSION below
# pins. pa11y-ci bundles its own Chromium through puppeteer, so nothing else in
# this repository has to know what a browser is.
PA11Y_CI_VERSION=4.0.1

# Node, only for the accessibility job. The repository's own toolchain has no
# Node in it: the stylesheet is generated by a standalone Tailwind binary and
# `go build` needs nothing else. This pin exists because pa11y-ci is an npm
# package, and nothing else in the tree is.
NODE_VERSION=24.21.0

# hey, the load-test driver scripts/loadtest.sh uses. Installed with
# `go install …@v$HEY_VERSION` into a throwaway GOBIN, so it is a tool and never
# a dependency: it does not appear in go.mod, and the static-binary promise
# does not depend on it.
HEY_VERSION=0.1.5
